WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:11.466
Good morning!

2
00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:14.408
Good morning!

3
00:00:14.409 --> 00:00:20.920
Who are you?

4
00:00:20.921 --> 00:00:23.971
I'm a groundhog.

5
00:00:23.972 --> 00:00:27.966
Groundhogs are big rodents.

6
00:00:27.967 --> 00:00:33.019
We're also called woodchucks.

7
00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:35.219
Where do you live?

8
00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:39.277
We live near fields and meadows.

9
00:00:39.278 --> 00:00:44.170
We usually stay close to forests.

10
00:00:44.171 --> 00:00:46.392
What do you eat?

11
00:00:46.393 --> 00:00:50.822
We like grasses, plants, and fruit.

12
00:00:50.823 --> 00:00:56.753
Sometimes we eat tree bark or bugs too.

13
00:00:56.754 --> 00:00:59.379
You eat a lot!

14
00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:03.376
We eat a lot in summer and fall.

15
00:01:03.377 --> 00:01:07.943
But we don't eat during winter.

16
00:01:07.944 --> 00:01:13.701
Groundhogs hibernate all winter long.

17
00:01:13.702 --> 00:01:17.157
Do you ever climb trees?

18
00:01:17.158 --> 00:01:22.122
Yes. We climb trees and bushes.

19
00:01:22.123 --> 00:01:25.669
We can swim too.

20
00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:28.565
Who are your enemies?

21
00:01:28.566 --> 00:01:32.458
Bears and foxes hunt us.

22
00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:36.004
So do wolves and birds.

23
00:01:36.005 --> 00:01:40.421
We hide from enemies underground.

24
00:01:40.422 --> 00:01:43.516
Do you dig holes?

25
00:01:43.517 --> 00:01:48.168
Yes! Groundhogs are good diggers.

26
00:01:48.169 --> 00:01:52.321
We use our claws to dig deep holes.

27
00:01:52.322 --> 00:01:58.511
Our holes have rooms and tunnels.

28
00:01:58.512 --> 00:02:02.141
Here comes a fox.

29
00:02:02.142 --> 00:02:05.518
Time to hide!

30
00:02:05.519 --> 00:02:09.934
Good-bye, Groundhog!
